// Testing/SpecVerdictSelfTest.maxon — WHAT A SPEC TEST IS WORTH WHEN ITS BINARY NEVER STARTED.
//
// ⭐⭐ **THIS RUNG GAVE THE SUITE A LANE THAT DELIBERATELY RUNS NOTHING**, and the whole danger of such
// a lane is that "we did not run it" is one careless simplification away from "it passed". A cross run
// on a host with no runner reports thousands of cases it never executed; if any of them ever lands in
// the passed column, or leaves a run that executed NOTHING reporting green, the lane stops being an
// instrument and becomes a very expensive way of printing OK.
//
// ⛔ **AND THE OPPOSITE DIRECTION IS THE DANGEROUS ONE.** Excusing a launch that FAILED — one that was
// ATTEMPTED and did not work — would wave through a program this compiler had just emitted and could
// not execute. That is precisely what running the program is for, so the guard asserts BOTH directions
// for EVERY supported target: the attempted-and-failed launch must be a FAIL everywhere, including on
// a lane whose other cases are legitimately unrun.
//
// ⭐ **IT IS THE BOOTSTRAP'S `SpecRunSelfTest` (maxon-sharp/Testing/SpecRunSelfTest.cs) RESTATED IN
// shv2's OWN TERMS, AND IT HAD TO BE RATHER THAN EXTENDED.** That file asserts the mapping over C# types
// in the C# compiler's process, against `TargetRunHost.WhyCannotRun`; it is run by `dotnet build` and it
// stays exactly as it is. It structurally cannot reach `TestOutcome`, `RunObservation` or
// `runStrategyFor`, which are the things this rung changed — a guard in the other compiler is not
// coverage of this one. The three properties it pins are the three pinned here, and the rows are named
// after its rows so the pair stays legible as one idea in two languages.
//
// ⚠ **NO SPEC CASE CAN REACH ANY OF THIS**, for the reason the C# one gives: a spec case is Maxon source
// the runner compiles, it cannot ask which host it is on, and a case that could would be red on some
// machine and green on another. So the assertions are made against SYNTHESIZED values — no compile, no
// spawn, no filesystem — and they ride the SUITE, in the parent, beside the other tree-level guards
// (`requireRunnerAvailable`, `requireLadderIndexComplete`, `requireBoardIdsUnique`). A check nobody runs
// is a claim.

// A synthesized case's names. They never reach a file: every row below is a pure function of a
// `TestOutcome`, a `GoldenDrift` or a `Target`.
let SelfTestSpecName = "self-test"
let SelfTestName = "verdict-mapping"

// How deep one failing row sits under the sentence that introduces it — `HarnessSelfTest`'s depth, for
// its reason: a reader takes the two panics as one shape.
let BrokenVerdictRowIndent = "\n  "

// ⭐ **PROVE THE NOT-RUN VERDICT IS STILL COUNTED, REASONED AND NOT GREEN.** Called ONCE by the suite's
// parent process, before a worker is spawned. It PANICS naming every row that failed — all of them
// together rather than the first, because one careless edit to `TestOutcome` breaks several and a
// report naming one sends the reader back for another sweep per remaining row.
export function requireSpecVerdictMapping()
	var broken = StringArray.create()

	checkLaunchFailureVerdicts(broken)
	checkNotRunHereIsNotGreen(broken)
	checkEveryOutcomeIsCounted(broken)
	checkOnlyAValidatedVerdictMints(broken)

	if broken.isEmpty() 'everyRowHeld'
		return
	end 'everyRowHeld'

	// ⚠ `panic` takes a STRING LITERAL — a `let`-bound String is rejected outright — so the list is
	// built as text and INTERPOLATED. Same constraint `HarnessSelfTest` and `LadderIndex` document.
	let report = indentedList(broken, indent: BrokenVerdictRowIndent)
	panic("SpecVerdictSelfTest: {broken.count()} row(s) of the not-run verdict mapping no longer hold. A lane whose whole job is reporting what it did NOT run is one simplification away from reporting that it passed.{report}")
end 'requireSpecVerdictMapping'

// ⭐ ROW 1 — a run this lane could not perform is `notRunHere`; a launch that FAILED is a `fail`.
//
// ASKED OF THE ROUTING, NOT RESTATED BESIDE IT. Which targets this host can execute is
// `runStrategyFor`'s answer (through `externalRunnerFor`, the one runner table), and spelling the rule
// here as its own `host.os == target.os` would be a second copy that agrees only by coincidence — the
// exact trap the C# row documents having sprung. So the EXPECTATION is derived from the strategy and
// what is asserted is the CONSEQUENCE: the observation that lane produces, mapped to a verdict.
function checkLaunchFailureVerdicts(broken StringArray)
	for target in supportedTargets() 'eachTarget'
		let key = targetToString(target)

		// ⛔ THE DANGEROUS DIRECTION, ASSERTED FOR EVERY TARGET WITHOUT EXCEPTION. A launch that was
		// ATTEMPTED and did not work is a defect in the binary, the runner or the OS, and it must be a
		// FAIL — including on a lane whose OTHER cases are legitimately unrun. Excusing it is how a
		// program this compiler had just emitted and could not start gets waved through.
		let attempted = verdictOf(RunObservation.failed("the OS refused it"), target: target)
		if not isFailVerdict(attempted) 'excusedAFailedLaunch'
			broken.push("{key}: a binary that FAILED TO LAUNCH earned '{verdictLine(attempted, label: key)}' instead of a FAIL. A launch that was attempted and did not work is a defect, and running the program is what exists to catch it.\n")
		end 'excusedAFailedLaunch'

		let unperformed = match runStrategyFor(target) 'lane'
			individually gives false
			wslBatch gives false
			noneHere gives true
		end 'lane'

		if not unperformed 'thisHostRunsIt'
			continue
		end 'thisHostRunsIt'

		// The OTHER direction, and only for the lanes that have it: this host performs no execution for
		// that target, so `executeRuns` answers `notRunnableHere` for every case that needed one. That
		// observation must be NOTRUN — neither a pass (nothing was proved) nor a failure of the case
		// (nothing about the case went wrong).
		let verdict = verdictOf(RunObservation.notRunnableHere, target: target)
		let named = match verdict 'v'
			notRunHere gives true
			pass gives false
			fail gives false
			skipped gives false
		end 'v'

		if not named 'wrongVerdict'
			broken.push("{key}: this host has no runner for it, so every case needing one is unperformed — and an unperformed execution must be NOTRUN. It was '{verdictLine(verdict, label: key)}'.\n")
		end 'wrongVerdict'
	end 'eachTarget'
end 'checkLaunchFailureVerdicts'

// Is this the FAIL arm specifically? `not isPass()` would not do: it is also true of the two not-run
// arms, which is exactly the confusion the row above exists to refuse.
function isFailVerdict(outcome TestOutcome) returns bool
	return match outcome 'v'
		fail gives true
		pass gives false
		skipped gives false
		notRunHere gives false
	end 'v'
end 'isFailVerdict'

// The verdict one observation earns, through the runner's own conversion. A `run` expectation with the
// simplest possible pins, because what is under test is the OBSERVATION arm and not the assertions.
function verdictOf(observation RunObservation, target Target) returns TestOutcome
	// `asyncTrace: false` — what is under test here is the OBSERVATION arm, and trace normalization is a
	// property of the stderr COMPARISON these unpinned expectations never reach.
	return checkObservedRun(SpecExitCode.unpinned, stderr: SpecStderr.unpinned, stdout: SpecStdout.unpinned, observation: observation, effectiveTarget: target, asyncTrace: false)
end 'verdictOf'

// ⭐ ROW 2 — a test nothing ran is not a pass, and a run whose every case was unperformed is not green.
// Asserted through `ResultTally`, which is where both facts are decided for every reporting path.
function checkNotRunHereIsNotGreen(broken StringArray)
	let tally = tallyResults(resultsOf(TestOutcome.notRunHere, golden: GoldenDrift.matched))

	if tally.passed != 0 'countedAsPassing'
		broken.push("a run of one NOTRUN case reports {tally.passed} passed. A test nothing executed is not a test that passed.\n")
	end 'countedAsPassing'

	if not tally.provedNothing() 'wouldExitGreen'
		broken.push("a run whose only case was NOTRUN does not report that it proved nothing, so it would exit 0. A gate that could not run is not a gate that passed.\n")
	end 'wouldExitGreen'
end 'checkNotRunHereIsNotGreen'

// ⭐ ROW 3 — every verdict lands in exactly one column. The totals come off ONE walk, so an outcome arm
// nobody counted makes them disagree with the number of results rather than hiding.
function checkEveryOutcomeIsCounted(broken StringArray)
	var results = SpecTestResultArray.create()
	results.append(resultsOf(TestOutcome.pass, golden: GoldenDrift.matched))
	results.append(resultsOf(TestOutcome.fail("a synthesized reason"), golden: GoldenDrift.notPinned))
	results.append(resultsOf(TestOutcome.skipped("a synthesized E3104"), golden: GoldenDrift.notPinned))
	results.append(resultsOf(TestOutcome.notRunHere, golden: GoldenDrift.unrecorded))

	let tally = tallyResults(results)
	if tally.total() == results.count() 'allCounted'
		return
	end 'allCounted'

	broken.push("{results.count()} results but {tally.total()} counted across passed/failed/skipped/not-run-here. A verdict that falls out of every column has been dropped from the report.\n")
end 'checkEveryOutcomeIsCounted'

// ⭐ ROW 4 — a verdict that was never established here may not WRITE a first golden, and one that was
// must still be able to. This is the half the C# guard states as `TargetRunHost.MintRefusalFor`, and it
// is the one that decides whether a cross lane's missing references get filled in with output nobody
// checked (see `SpecTestRunner.recordFragmentAndCleanup` for the 810 measured cases where they were).
function checkOnlyAValidatedVerdictMints(broken StringArray)
	if TestOutcome.notRunHere.isPass() 'wouldMint'
		broken.push("a NOTRUN verdict reports itself as a pass, so it would be allowed to MINT a golden from a program nobody executed — and that golden then becomes what a real run on a real host is compared against.\n")
	end 'wouldMint'

	if not TestOutcome.notRunHere.pinsEmittedCode() 'wouldNotCompare'
		broken.push("a NOTRUN verdict does not pin its emitted code, so its committed golden would never be compared. That comparison is the ONLY verification such a case can get on this host, and it is what the whole lane is for.\n")
	end 'wouldNotCompare'

	if not TestOutcome.pass.pinsEmittedCode() 'passLostItsGolden'
		broken.push("a PASSING verdict does not pin its emitted code, so no golden would be compared on any lane at all.\n")
	end 'passLostItsGolden'
end 'checkOnlyAValidatedVerdictMints'

// One synthesized result, as the one-element list every row above works over.
function resultsOf(outcome TestOutcome, golden GoldenDrift) returns SpecTestResultArray
	var results = SpecTestResultArray.create()
	results.push(SpecTestResult.create(SelfTestSpecName, testName: SelfTestName, outcome: outcome, golden: golden))
	return results
end 'resultsOf'
